(A loop variable over a list of lists holds its own copy of each element,
 and a list parameter given it works on that copy, which the rest of the
 loop body sees. The list being walked is untouched.)
To 'mark' with a list called items.
    append "x" to items.

a list called outer is [["a"], ["b"]].
For each inner in outer, 'mark' of inner, Print "inner: {inner}".
Print "outer: {outer}".
